{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to Heap as custom events, through its server-side bulk track API.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"HeapEncoding","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"HeapEncoding"}],"title":"HeapEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/heap(appID:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for Heap in one call. It checks your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"environment’s app ID, then posts to the track endpoint of your project’s data center,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/heapanalytics.com\/api\/track"},{"type":"text","text":" or, for the EU, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/c.eu.heap-api.com\/api\/track"},{"type":"text","text":", with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Each batch is split to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": 1,000 events a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request, the most Heap’s bulk track API takes, and 1,000,000 bytes a request, the encoder’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound, as Heap documents none. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Heap’s server-side API complements its SDKs: Heap says “you can only send events to identified","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"users”. Every user this destination makes has only server-side events, and Heap treats such a user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"differently from one its SDKs capture:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the user’s profile says its events are hidden, and Heap lists them under the Hidden Events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"category of its Events tab;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the events aren’t sessionized, so Heap’s Sessions list stays empty for them;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a session filter on a user property sees only SDK sessions, so it matches none of them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So checking that events reach Heap’s Live data feed isn’t enough: after setting the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"up, confirm that its events appear in the charts and reports you mean to use.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The track API takes the app ID alone, which Heap’s own SDKs ship inside every app, and no API key,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to Heap directly. Heap’s API key is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for its user deletion API, which this module doesn’t call; don’t put one in an app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import HeapEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let heap = try HTTPDestination.heap(","    appID: appID,  \/\/ the environment's ID, from Heap's project settings","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: heap)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapSetupError"},{"text":" for an app ID that is empty or only whitespace, and for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holding anything but ASCII digits: a Heap environment’s ID is a number, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"12343283"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"text":" has no default. Pass ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapRegion\/eu"},{"text":" when your project’s data is in Heap’s EU data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"center.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Users-are-sessions","text":"Users are sessions","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Heap files each event under its ","type":"text"},{"code":"identity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and makes a user for each identity it hasn’t seen. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination sends the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, as the identity: its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as a lowercase UUID. Nothing else identifies a record: no ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vendor identifier, device identifier or account, and no trace context.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"So Heap’s users are sessions. A person who opens the app three times is three users, and Heap’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retention and user counts describe sessions, not people. That is the library’s default, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"privacy. To count","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"devices or accounts instead, write your own enricher and encoder that send the identifier you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose; this encoder sends the session alone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record with no session, from a tracker without the sessions enricher, is its own user: its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity is the record’s identifier. A record a store recovered after a relaunch keeps its session. Making up a session would join unrelated records, skipping"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the record would lose it, and Heap takes no event without an identity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-Heap-receives","text":"What Heap receives","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each request is a JSON object: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app_id"},{"type":"text","text":", as given, without surrounding whitespace, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one track event per record. Every event has:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the event’s name;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"identity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the session;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"idempotency_key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the record’s identifier, so Heap stores a record sent twice under the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity once. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes under","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the identity of its first send, and Heap stores it once;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so an event sent late still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counts at the time it was tracked;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when the event has any to send."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made with. Heap takes a number or a string as a property’s value, so an object or array is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flattened into dotted names: a "},{"code":"cart","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holding "},{"code":"size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"cart.size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the first element of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"tags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"tags.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A boolean is the string "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a number keeps its JSON type, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property is left out. A "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context isn’t sent. Heap keeps no built-in property of an event sent through its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server-side API, so the app’s version or the device’s model would sit among the event’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties, where they could collide with your own names.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","text":"Records left out","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name is longer than the 1,024 characters Heap takes;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a property named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_name"},{"type":"text","text":", which Heap reserves: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first two are fields of a track request, and the last is the screen name its mobile SDKs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capture. A name like one, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"User_id"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_name.0"},{"type":"text","text":", is sent."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a property, once flattened, whose name or string value is 1,024 characters or more:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Heap takes fewer. Characters are counted in UTF-16, as JavaScript counts them, so an emoji"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counts two."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999, which have no four-digit ISO 8601 year;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one too large for a request of 1,000,000 bytes on its own.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the plan whose name would be left out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"What-Heap-doesnt-report","text":"What Heap doesn’t report","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Heap answers 200 to a request it takes and 400 to one it can’t, which the destination drops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports with every record of the request. Its docs don’t say what it answers to an app ID of no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"environment, so confirm that the first events appear in your charts after setting it up.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Heap takes 15,000 events a minute from one environment, and every device sending to it shares","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that limit: at a steady rate it is about 21.6 million events a day across all your users, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"burst, such as many devices sending their backlogs at once, reaches it sooner. Heap’s docs don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"say what it answers past the limit. If it answers 429, the destination retries the request on its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backoff, with full jitter, so devices refused together retry at different moments. It doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Retry-After"},{"text":", though, so a backlog can still grow. If it answers 400, the destination drops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole request and reports it as rejected, and its records are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Heap also takes 30 requests in 30 seconds and 1,000 events a minute from one identity, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one session here. A session whose own backlog holds more than 1,000 events, such as one that ran"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"long offline, goes past it when it sends, with the same outcomes. A smaller batch wouldn’t avoid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that, as the destination doesn’t pace its requests, so requests keep Heap’s bulk maximum of 1,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Events sent through the server-side API carry only the properties sent with them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Heap receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/heap(appID:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/heap(appID:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapRegion","doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Heap","title":"Sending to Heap"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/heapencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://HeapEncoding/documentation/HeapEncoding/HeapEncodingError":{"type":"topic","title":"HeapEncodingError","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeapEncodingError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/heapencoding\/heapencodingerror","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapEncodingError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s requests as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no record of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeapEncodingError"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","title":"Choosing Destinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"text":"Choosing Destinations","type":"text"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://HeapEncoding/documentation/HeapEncoding/HeapBatchEncoder/init(appID:plan:limit:)":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/heapencoding\/heapbatchencoder\/init(appid:plan:limit:)","abstract":[{"text":"An encoder of the events ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" describes, for the Heap environment ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", splitting each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"limit"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"init(appID:plan:limit:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"limit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HeapSetupError","preciseIdentifier":"s:12HeapEncoding0A10SetupErrorO"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HeapBatchEncoder\/init(appID:plan:limit:)"},"doc://HeapEncoding/documentation/HeapEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/heap(appID:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeapEncoding\/documentation\/HeapEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/heap(appID:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Heap environment ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appID"},{"text":", whose data resides in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"text":", through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"heap(appID:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"heap"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12HeapEncoding0A6RegionO","text":"HeapRegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12HeapEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","text":"HeapSetupError"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12HeapEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","text":"HeapBatchEncoder"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"url":"\/documentation\/heapencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/heap(appid:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"kin